---
title: Prefabs
---
A piece of map designed by hand, dropped into a generated one [[t:198-200 s:22]].

## The rule
{% table label="Where a prefab goes, by placement" rowheads=true %}
* Placement
* How
---
* `room` (c14)
* pick random rooms until one is big enough; stamp the prefab at that room’s center [[c14:104-124]]
---
* `open-area` (c15)
* pick random spots until the whole prefab lies on floor; stamp it there [[c15:41-67]]
---
* `center` (c09)
* stamp it over the center columns of the map [[c09:116-133]]
{% /table %}

- **Talk says:** on a map with rooms, go through the room list and find a room that’s bigger than the prefab [[t:203-205]].
- **Talk says:** on a map without rooms, pick random locations and see if the prefab will fit [[t:205-207]].

## Step-through
@@steps limit=5

## Controls
@@control shape
`vault`: the talk’s treasure ringed by traps [[c14:86-102 c14:149-155 t:200-201]]. `spine`: our stand-in for the fortifications the talk’s combined map gets, a hall of our own design [[own]].
@@control place
`room`: the center of a random room that is big enough [[c14:104-124]]. `open-area`: wherever a random spot has floor under all of it [[c15:41-67]]. `center`: down the middle of the map, as the combined map’s is [[c09:116-133]].

## Measured traits
@@measured

- **Vault:** changes none of the traits its map had [[own]].
  - **Why:** treasure and traps count as walkable [[own]].

## Failures
@@fails

- **No cap in the talk’s code:** both of its placement loops end only when the prefab has been placed [[c14:104-124 c15:41-67]].
- **So:** on a map with no room big enough, or no clear patch of floor the right size, they never end [[own]].
- **Ours:** stops and records the seed [[own]].

